From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonny Heggheim <hegjon@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:28:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: x1e80100: Raise the speaker caps for
 the Galaxy Book4 Edge 14

The Samsung Galaxy Book4 Edge 14 has WSA883x speaker amplifiers, where
the PA Volume cap of 6 meant for WSA884x is -3 dB rather than 0 dB, and
its speakers come out far below Windows. Cap PA Volume at 17, 0 dB
on WSA883x and the cap sc8280xp uses for the same amplifiers, and
Digital Volume at 84 (0 dB), the value its four-speaker UCM requests.

[birk: from github.com/hegjon/omarchy-galaxy-book4-edge at ab22862,
 gb4e/snd-soc-x1e80100-gb4e/x1e80100-gb4e-volume.patch, rebased on the
 Zenbook A16 branch and matched on the 14-inch compatible only, since
 nobody has checked the 16-inch model's amplifiers]

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
index 0c752d8b0..c5b828f84 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
@@ -58,6 +58,11 @@ static int x1e80100_snd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 		 * PA Volume does not change the output, so raising that cap
 		 * would buy nothing; the digital cap was what held a full-scale
 		 * signal 3 dB short of the amplifiers' full scale.
+		 *
+		 * The Samsung Galaxy Book4 Edge 14 has WSA883x amplifiers, whose
+		 * PA Volume steps differ: 6 is -3 dB there and 17 is 0 dB, the
+		 * cap sc8280xp uses for the same amplifiers. Digital Volume is
+		 * allowed to 0 dB (84), the value its four-speaker UCM requests.
 		 */
 		if (of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,denali")) {
 			digital_max = 84;
@@ -65,6 +70,9 @@ static int x1e80100_snd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 		} else if (of_machine_is_compatible("asus,zenbook-a16-ux3607oa")) {
 			digital_max = 84;
 			pa_max = 6;
+		} else if (of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,galaxy-book4-edge-14")) {
+			digital_max = 84;
+			pa_max = 17;
 		} else {
 			digital_max = 81;
 			pa_max = 6;
